From: Kirn Gill II <segin2005@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 9 Jun 2026 13:36:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/83] =?UTF-8?q?kernel:=20dtcm=20no=20longer=20freezes=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?the=20UI=20=E2=80=94=20preemptible=20USB=20poll=20wait=20+=20gu?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ard=20signals=20to=20user=20mode?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Opening dtcm (or any sustained activity) could freeze the entire desktop.
gdb showed the CPU monopolised by usb_hid_poll_thread busy-spinning in
uhci_poll_td: it pause-loops up to the 5s transfer deadline, and the HID
poll kthread runs with interrupts DISABLED (switch_to doesn't save/restore
EFLAGS, so a kthread that never re-enables IF stays IF=0).  With interrupts
off the timer can't fire, nothing preempts the spin, and a wedged HID
transfer starves the X server and its clients — dtcm/Xfbdev sit READY but
never run.

Fix, two parts:
- uhci.c: run uhci_poll_td's completion wait with interrupts enabled
  (intr_disable/intr_enable around the loop, intr_restore on exit) so the
  timer tick can preempt it; the controller still completes the TD via DMA.
- idt.c: only call signal_handle_pending() when the interrupt came from
  user mode.  Enabling preemption of the kthread exposed a latent crash:
  the timer IRQ would preempt the kthread, and on return the unguarded
  signal_handle_pending(regs) ran for a kernel-mode frame whose `regs`
  pointer had been clobbered across the sched_yield -> page-fault panic in
  signal_handle_pending (regs->cs deref).  Signals are only ever delivered
  on return to user mode, so the kernel-frame call was always a no-op
  anyway; gating it on is_usermode removes both the crash and a needless
  deref. (This is why the kthread defensively ran with IF=0 before.)

Verified: dtcm opens, the desktop reaches steady state with the CPU idle
(swapper/hlt) instead of monopolised, no panic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sys/arch/i386/idt.c    |  4 ++--
 sys/drivers/usb/uhci.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sys/arch/i386/idt.c b/sys/arch/i386/idt.c
index 4633cf8b..0ab20dfa 100644
--- a/sys/arch/i386/idt.c
+++ b/sys/arch/i386/idt.c
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@ void isr_handler(registers_t *regs) {
         } else if (!current_thread && is_usermode) {
             sched_yield();
         }
-        signal_handle_pending(regs);
+        if (is_usermode) signal_handle_pending(regs);  /* not for kernel-mode IRQs */
         return;
     }
 
@@ -540,5 +540,5 @@ void isr_handler(registers_t *regs) {
         outb(0x20, 0x20);
     }
 
-    signal_handle_pending(regs);
+    if (is_usermode) signal_handle_pending(regs);  /* not for kernel-mode IRQs */
 }
diff --git a/sys/drivers/usb/uhci.c b/sys/drivers/usb/uhci.c
index 79393717..a89f2a88 100644
--- a/sys/drivers/usb/uhci.c
+++ b/sys/drivers/usb/uhci.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <sys/dma.h>
 #include <sys/irq.h>
 #include <sys/lock.h>
+#include <intr.h>
 #include <vm/vm_kmem.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
@@ -409,12 +410,23 @@ static int uhci_poll_td(uhci_hc_t *hc, struct uhci_td *td,
     (void)hc;
 
     while (td && walk_budget--) {
-        /* Poll until this TD is no longer active */
+        /* Poll until this TD is no longer active.  Run the wait with
+         * interrupts ENABLED so the timer tick can preempt us.  The HID poll
+         * kthread runs with IF=0 (switch_to doesn't save/restore EFLAGS), so a
+         * bare pause-spin here is never preempted: a wedged transfer would
+         * monopolise the CPU for the full 5 s timeout and freeze the whole UI
+         * (opening dtcm reproduced it).  Enabling interrupts lets the X server
+         * and its clients keep running while the controller works. */
+        uint32_t _saved_if = intr_disable();
+        intr_enable();
         while (td->ctrl_status & UHCI_TD_CTRL_ACTIVE) {
-            if ((uint64_t)get_uptime_ms() > deadline)
+            if ((uint64_t)get_uptime_ms() > deadline) {
+                intr_restore(_saved_if);
                 return USB_XFER_TIMEOUT;
+            }
             __asm__ volatile("pause");
         }
+        intr_restore(_saved_if);
 
         /* Check for errors */
         if (td->ctrl_status & UHCI_TD_CTRL_STALLED) {
-- 
